# Pleo git & commits

## After every phase

When a phase’s **live-test exit gate PASSes**, create a git commit for that phase’s work before starting the next phase.

- Message style: `Phase N: <short why>` (e.g. `Phase 1: prove generic extraction and React-safe writeback`)
- Include phase code, docs updates, and test/review artifacts that belong in the repo
- Do **not** commit secrets, API keys, or `node_modules`

## Author identity (mandatory)

- Commits must be authored as **Darshan Harihar** / the user’s GitHub account (`DarshanHarihar1`)
- Use the existing git `user.name` / `user.email` already configured on the machine
- **Never** run `git config` to change identity
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by:` (Cursor, Copilot, or any AI)
- **Never** put “Cursor”, “copilot”, or agent names in the commit message body or trailers
- If a hook or tool appends `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`, **do not leave it**. Create a clean commit with `git commit-tree` (same tree, author/committer = Darshan Harihar) and `git reset --hard` to it; if already pushed, `git push --force-with-lease` only to strip that trailer on an otherwise-empty history rewrite the user already authorized via this rule.
- Verify with: `git log -1 --format=%B` — must not contain `Co-authored-by` or `Cursor`

## Remote

- Repo: `https://github.com/DarshanHarihar1/pleo.git`
- Push phase commits when the user asks, or after phase commit if they already requested ongoing remote sync
